# Cloudflare Pages proxy rules — copy this file to web/_redirects and fill in
# the real Render service hostname before publishing.
#
# The Pages domain serves the static app; every API and storage request must
# reach the Render backend as SAME-ORIGIN so the browser never talks to a
# second origin (no CORS involvement, cookies/Authorization stay first-party).
#
# Replace YOUR-RENDER-SERVICE with the service name Render assigns, e.g.
#   https://studybridge-api.onrender.com
#
# /functions/v1/app/*  — the whole application API (the same path the deployed
#                         Edge Function used, so config and code need no change).
# /storage/*           — server-issued signed upload/download capability URLs.
#                         The browser PUTs uploads straight to them; the token
#                         is validated by the backend, never by Cloudflare.
#
# 200 means "proxy, keep the client URL". These rules never rewrite the address
# bar, and no secret value belongs in this file or in any Pages environment
# variable — the anon key travels inside web/js/config.js only.
#
# ORDER MATTERS: Pages applies the first matching rule, so these two lines must
# come before any catch-all.

/functions/v1/app/* https://YOUR-RENDER-SERVICE.onrender.com/functions/v1/app/:splat 200
/storage/* https://YOUR-RENDER-SERVICE.onrender.com/storage/:splat 200
